These fixtures have labels at the ends of edges (cardinalities), which the
port hands to ELK as head and tail labels. They are byte-identical once
moon_elk

- writes edge labels back by origin rather than by position: until then
  every label of such an edge gets the geometry of another one;
- stacks the labels of a self loop by the direction the graph was given
  (self_loop_lr, random_self_loop): until then a self loop with two labels
  in a graph laid out to the right or left gets them side by side.

Remove this file, and the `#skip` in tests/class_test.mbt, when the layout
engine in use has both fixes.
